# Java Style Guide

## Naming Conventions

### Classes
- **PascalCase**, nouns
- Suffix by type: `UserService`, `UserController`, `UserMapper`

### Methods
- **camelCase**, verbs
- `findById()`, `createUser()`, `isValid()`

### Variables
- **camelCase**, descriptive
- Boolean prefix: `isActive`, `hasPermission`, `canDelete`

### Constants
- **UPPER_SNAKE_CASE**
- `MAX_RETRY_COUNT`, `DEFAULT_PAGE_SIZE`

## Code Structure

### Method Size
- **Max 20 lines** per method
- Extract helper methods if larger

### Parameters
- **Max 3 parameters**
- Use object for more: `createUser(CreateUserRequest request)`

### Return Early
```java
// GOOD
public User findById(Long id) {
    if (id == null) {
        throw new IllegalArgumentException("ID required");
    }
    return repository.findById(id)
        .orElseThrow(() -> new UserNotFoundException(id));
}

// AVOID - nested conditionals
public User findById(Long id) {
    if (id != null) {
        Optional<User> user = repository.findById(id);
        if (user.isPresent()) {
            return user.get();
        } else {
            throw new UserNotFoundException(id);
        }
    } else {
        throw new IllegalArgumentException("ID required");
    }
}
```

## Formatting

### Indentation
- 4 spaces (no tabs)

### Line Length
- Max 120 characters

### Imports
- No wildcard imports
- Order: java -> javax -> third-party -> project

### Braces
```java
// Same line opening brace
if (condition) {
    doSomething();
} else {
    doOther();
}

// Single statement - still use braces
if (condition) {
    return early;
}
```

## Documentation

### When to Comment
- **WHY**, not what
- Complex business rules
- Non-obvious algorithms

### JavaDoc
```java
/**
 * Applies promotional discount for eligible users.
 * Eligibility: premium users with 5+ purchases in last 30 days.
 *
 * @param user the user to check
 * @return discount percentage (0-100)
 * @throws UserNotFoundException if user not found
 */
public int calculateDiscount(User user) { }
```

## Clean Code Principles

### Single Responsibility
```java
// BAD - multiple concerns
class UserService {
    void saveUser(User user) { }
    void sendEmail(String email) { }  // Not user concern
}

// GOOD - separated
class UserService {
    void saveUser(User user) { }
}
class EmailService {
    void sendEmail(String email) { }
}
```

### DRY - Don't Repeat Yourself
```java
// BAD - duplicated validation
void validateUser(User user) {
    if (user.getEmail() == null) throw new ValidationException("Email required");
}
void validateAdmin(Admin admin) {
    if (admin.getEmail() == null) throw new ValidationException("Email required");
}

// GOOD - extracted
void validateEmail(String email) {
    if (email == null) throw new ValidationException("Email required");
}
```

### Avoid Magic Values
```java
// BAD
if (user.getRole() == 1) { }

// GOOD
if (user.getRole() == UserRole.ADMIN) { }
```
